CONTEXT Cleanup INCLUDES Orders FROM "../contexts/orders.adl"
CONTEXT Cleanup IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Cleanup
{+ A context relaxes two invariants of the context it includes, by assigning them to a role.
Its population violates both, which the context Orders itself would refuse.
The compiler adds, for each of the two rules, a relation that registers what satisfies it
and a blocking invariant that keeps what is registered from violating it again.
This context shows the registered orders in an interface. +}

ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS Orders.hasCustomer, Orders.deliveredAtCustomer

POPULATION Orders.customer[Orders.Order*Orders.Customer] CONTAINS [ ("o1", "Ada") ]
POPULATION Orders.address[Orders.Customer*Orders.Address] CONTAINS [ ("Ada", "Main Street 1") ]
POPULATION Orders.delivered[Orders.Order*Orders.Address] CONTAINS
  [ ("o1", "Main Street 1")
  ; ("o2", "Harbour Road 2")
  ]

INTERFACE Work FOR Clerk : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*Orders.Order] cRud BOX
  [ "order" : I cRud
  , "has a customer" : fixedHasCustomer cRud
  , "delivered at its customer" : fixedDeliveredAtCustomer cRud
  ]

ENDCONTEXT
